## Steering (no need to interrupt)

- **Reorder / edit / insert work:** edit `openspec/backlog.md`. The loop always takes the topmost unchecked `- [ ]` on its next iteration.
- **Emergency stop:** `touch openspec/STOP`. The loop halts before starting the next increment. Delete the file to resume.
- **Hard stop now:** interrupt the running `/loop` (Esc), or tell it to stop.

## Merge guard

`.claude/hooks/merge-guard.sh` runs as a `PreToolUse` hook on every Bash call and independently re-checks every `gh pr merge`: all checks green, newest `### 🤖` gate review reads PASS. Mode lives in `.claude/hooks/merge-guard.mode` (`off | log | enforce-ci | enforce`), re-read on every invocation — no restart needed.

**Trust ramp.** It starts in `log` so it cannot block a real merge before you have seen it agree with the loop. After an increment or two:

```bash
cut -f2,5,6 .claude/hooks/merge-guard.log   # every merge the loop performed should show ALLOW
echo enforce > .claude/hooks/merge-guard.mode
```

From then on "never force-merge" is enforced by the harness rather than trusted to the model.

## When it escalates

The loop prints a `⛔ ESCALATION` block and stops when it can't safely proceed: CI still red after 2 fix cycles, a gate BLOCK or twice-unresolved REVISE/CHANGES, a worker returning FAILED, an unmet `needs-human:` precondition, a merge-guard denial, or dirty git state. Read the block, make the one decision it asks for, then relaunch `/loop /kmp-forge-next-increment`.
